Subject: [PATCH 05/16] feat(client): the game starts at the menu - host
 construction deferred (PLAN-M10.2 3.2)

App now carries the content tree (the New Match screen lists its maps)
and the screens::AppState machine; the match host is Option<MatchHost>,
built only when Start is pressed (begin_match: bundle the selected map,
build the mode's setup, fresh controllers, reset every match-scoped
state - the A15 drop + reconstruct discipline, determinism unchanged)
and dropped on Quit to Menu (drop_match: everything clears - a
menu-only session never panics, writes a report, or submits a command).

- input routing: menus own the pointer and the keyboard (hover moves
  focus, click activates, arrows + Enter navigate, Esc backs out);
  world input lives only in InMatch; stale camera keys clear at menus.
- submit_order guards twice: spectate is a silent no-op (A-113) and no
  order ever leaves a menu.
- --record: a menu-only session records nothing; the exit hook's write
  is host-guarded. --frames at the menu reports the menu honestly (T7).
- --seed becomes the New Match field's prefill (Option: absent or
  malformed = the field starts random, A-111's std RandomState source,
  never the sim's RNG); windowed_summary prints the prefill.
- windowed_summary, F8 dump, P pause, '.' single-step, and the end-screen
  promotion (InMatch -> EndScreen when the host reports an outcome) all
  host-guarded. Edge scroll and key pan only run in-match.
- the main menu frame (title over a dimmed, matchless world) renders
  through the existing overlay pass; the button list lands next.

