From 1a2baa38b816a34b084ecca2869c286597c9d9fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elieaazzam-art <elieaazzam-art@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:29:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] feat(client): the menu pass - panels, rows, focus ring,
 hit rects (PLAN-M10.2 3.6)

ui::build_menu renders every screen the state machine navigates:
solid panels with the blue border, rows with the label left and the
value right, the focused row brightened with the focus ring (hover
moves the same focus the keyboard moves - one visual for both input
paths), the Phase 2 blue/orange accents, and hit rects in focus-index
order so the machine's activate_index and the pixel geometry agree by
construction. The New Match screen shows the mode (cycling), the seed
(random hint or the typed digits), and the map list; the settings
screen shows all seven keys with their values and the Phase 4 note on
master volume plus the adjust/save hint; the end screen reuses the M8
headline law (VICTORY green / DEFEAT red). draw_menu_frame (no host)
and the live-match path (pause/end/settings-over-pause - dimmed
backdrop over the world) both build through the same pass. 3 new tests
(the button ids match the machine's focus indices on every screen, the
rects are real and disjoint, the field rows render).
