+- **M10.2 Phase 3: the config file is hand-rolled and forgiving.** `client/src/config.rs` parses `key=value` lines with `#` comments (no serde, no `dirs` — the allow-list is untouched); a malformed value costs only its own key (per-key salvage, A-108); unknown keys are ignored; values range-clamp. The directory comes from `std::env` (XDG/HOME/APPDATA per platform, A-109) and a machine with none of them runs on in-memory defaults with persistence silently disabled — never a panic. Save timing: Done saves, Esc leaves without saving (A-115, documented on the screen itself).
+
+- **M10.2 Phase 3: zero-entity frames exposed a latent wgpu bug.** The fog pass leaves the *fog* bind group in slot 0; the decal pass between it and the entity draw restores the camera group, but it is skipped when there is nothing to draw — and a menu frame with zero entities is exactly that (mutual destruction would also have hit it). wgpu validates bind groups even for a zero-instance draw; `render()` now re-binds the camera group before the entity draw.
+
+- **M10.2 Phase 3: XTEST driver discipline.** Keys sent faster than ~0.3 s apart can be processed against stale screen state under llvmpipe load (the first settings-persistence run "failed" because of a too-tight key cadence and a driver arg-order bug — the app was fine). Use ≥0.25–0.4 s per key, pass mode-specific CLI args BEFORE `Popen`, and verify the seed in the evidence lines (the smoke summary and the live match-ended line both print it). The graceful close (WM_DELETE_WINDOW ClientMessage, 32-bit data) exits the app cleanly with its exit-state line.
